 "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet IP gateway",
 "applies_to": "Lennox VRF P3 outdoor and indoor units in VRB and VPB systems.",
 "summary": "The V0CTRL95P-3 connects Lennox VRF systems to a BMS over BACnet IP, with four RS-485 buses to the VRF units and an Ethernet port. Each indoor and outdoor unit appears as its own BACnet device whose device ID encodes the bus, unit type and unit address; inside each device the object instances are fixed, so one indoor template and one outdoor template cover the site. Indoor units take on/off, mode, fan speed and setpoint commands; outdoor units are mostly monitoring plus an emergency stop.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Device ID = 4 digits: bus (port) 0-3, unit type (0 = indoor, 1 = outdoor), unit address (indoor 00-63, outdoor 00-31). Example from the guide: 0001 = bus 0, indoor unit 01.",
  "The list holds two object sets: indoor unit devices (first 18 rows) and outdoor unit devices (last 24 rows). Instances repeat between the two (e.g. AI 1 is room temperature on an indoor unit and ambient temperature on an outdoor unit).",
  "The guide gives setpoint ranges as 62-86 °F (17-30 °C) and does not say which unit the gateway reports.",
  "Fan speed and fan lock values pair several codes per speed (1-2 low, 3-4 medium, 5-7 high).",
  "The gateway is rated for up to 320 VRB/VPB systems, 960 outdoor units and 2560 indoor units; the guide's Appendix A with the details is not part of this document."
 ],
